{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>For he did not know that she was his daughter-in-law.</b> Even after he turned aside to her on the road, he did not recognize her — for had he recognized her he would have spoken with her concerning his son. But unto El, blessed be He, there were arranged circumstances such that He desired her seed to come from Judah, who was more complete and acceptable than Shelah, and from her would come the Messiah of our righteousness." "<b>What will you give me.</b> She began to speak so that he might recognize her, for she was not intent on any hire whatsoever, but her intent was to raise up seed from Judah. Accordingly she took a pledge — not to benefit from it but for a testimony; and had he given her a hire she would not have accepted it, for then there would have been no testimony with her to justify herself."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:33:50.751584235Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}